+// Per-row structured-output constraint for one decode or prefill-finalization unit.
+//
+// `token_mask` is the host LSB-first bitset over the target token domain for the row's next sampled
+// position, produced by the Frontend output session that owns the request. An empty span means the
+// row samples from the unconstrained domain for this unit, which is how a constraint that is dormant
+// (the model is still in its reasoning channel) is expressed.
+//
+// The span is a *host* view on purpose. The Engine produces it and owns its lifetime across the
+// Program call, and the Program decides where the device copy lives — putting a device address in a
+// package-neutral contract type would make device memory Engine-visible, which is what token_counts
+// deliberately avoids.
+struct RoundConstraint {
+    std::span<const std::uint8_t> token_mask;
+    // True when the request owns a constraint at all, whether or not this unit carries a mask yet.
+    //
+    // A mask describes exactly one position: the grammar advances one token at a time, and the
+    // sampler applies a single per-row configuration to every column of a speculative unit. A draft
+    // column would therefore be sampled against a state it has already moved past, so a constrained
+    // row is decoded one token per unit — the mask is exact there and no unit is ever partially
+    // accepted, which the Engine's licensed-prefix contract does not permit outside a finish.
+    //
+    // The flag is separate from `token_mask` because dormancy is not absence: while the model is
+    // still reasoning the mask is empty, yet the unit that carries the reasoning close marker is
+    // precisely the one whose trailing columns would escape the constraint.
+    bool constrained = false;
+};
